KZ3 patch 1130 (SPU pass 108 part 3; upstream candidate): v0.18.0's spu_coh_bitmap.h defines g_spu_coh_bits in the
header, `__declspec(selectany)` on MSVC and `__attribute__((weak))` elsewhere, meaning one merged definition. MinGW's GNU
ld (PE/COFF weak externals) does not merge them: every object that includes the header gets its own
`.weak.g_spu_coh_bits.<symbol>` storage (shown with x86_64-w64-mingw32-nm on a two-file test: two BSS slots), so the
PPU store paths in ppu_loader.cpp read a NULL copy spu_coherency.c never publishes (PPU stores would never see a
reserved line), and the lifted PPU code's plain `extern` (ppu_recomp.h) failed to link (undefined reference). Fix: on
MinGW (_WIN32 without _MSC_VER) the header declares it extern and spu_coherency.c holds the one strong definition.
MSVC (selectany) and ELF (weak, merged) are unchanged.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h b/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h
index 79bffe73..d716d110 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_coh_bitmap.h
@@ -31,7 +31,14 @@ extern "C" {
 
 /* One bit per line over the 32-bit guest address space; spu_coherency.c
  * publishes it on the first reservation and only ever sets bits. */
+#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(_MSC_VER)
+/* KZ3 patch 1130: MinGW (GNU ld, PE/COFF) does not merge weak definitions: each object gets its own
+ * `.weak.g_spu_coh_bits.<symbol>` storage, so the PPU store paths (ppu_loader.cpp) read a copy spu_coherency.c
+ * never publishes, and a plain `extern` reference finds no definition at all. One strong definition there. */
+extern const unsigned char* g_spu_coh_bits;
+#else
 SPU_COH_SHARED const unsigned char* g_spu_coh_bits = 0;
+#endif
 
 static inline int spu_coh_line_reserved(uint32_t addr)
 {
diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_coherency.c b/runtime/spu/spu_coherency.c
index 0e4beb37..d778cc55 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_coherency.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_coherency.c
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include "spu_coherency.h"
 #include "spu_coh_bitmap.h"
+#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(_MSC_VER)
+const unsigned char* g_spu_coh_bits = 0;   /* KZ3 patch 1130: the one MinGW definition (spu_coh_bitmap.h) */
+#endif
 
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
